  "recipeCuisine": "Malaysia",
  "name": "Chinese Clay Pot Rice with Chicken",
  "text": "Chinese Clay Pot Rice with Chicken\n\nYield: 4\n\nPreparation time:\n\nCooking time:\n\nIngredients\n\n500 g chicken breast fillets,\n\n5 dried shiitake mushrooms (soaked inn hot water for 30 minutes until soft),\n\n1 Chinese sausage (sliced),\n\n750 ml chicken stock,\n\n225 g long grain rice (washed and drained),\n\nFresh coriander leaves (chopped for the garnish).\n\nFor the marinade\n\n2 tbsp sesame oil,\n\n3 tbsp oyster sauce,\n\n2 tbsp soy sauce,\n\n25 g fresh root ginger (finely grated),\n\n2 spring onions (trimmed and finely sliced),\n\n1 red chilli (deseeded and finely sliced),\n\n1 tsp sugar,\n\nGround black pepper.\n\nPreparation\n\n1. Mix together the ingredients for the marinade and toss in the chicken. Set aside.\n\n2. Squeeze the water out of the soaked mushrooms, and with a sharp knife trim any hard stems, and halve.\n\n3. Add the mushrooms and the sausage to the marinating chicken.\n\n4. Bring the stock to the boil.\n\n5. Stir in the rice and bring back to the boil.\n\n6. Reduce to a simmer and cook for 15-20 minutes until almost all of the liquid has been absorbed.\n\n7. Spread the chicken and marinade mixture over the top of the rice.\n\n8. Leave to steam for 10-15 minutes until the chicken has been cooked.\n\n9. Garnish with coriander and serve.",
  "recipeYield": "4",
  "recipeIngredient": [
    "500 g chicken breast fillets,",
    "5 dried shiitake mushrooms (soaked inn hot water for 30 minutes until soft),",
    "1 Chinese sausage (sliced),",
    "750 ml chicken stock,",
    "225 g long grain rice (washed and drained),",
    "Fresh coriander leaves (chopped for the garnish).",
